                                                "sense_id": "accf4a7f-5bd7-3717-bc68-cd5464c0bae1",
                                                "text": "[Jeremy O. Harris:] One of the things I worry about is that the little gay boys and girls I’m friends with don’t meet people their age IRL. They only know people through their oomfs, right? The oomfs run the world.\n[Devan Shimoyama:] What’s “oomf”?\n[Jeremy O. Harris:] An oomf is an “O.O.M.F.” — “one of my friends,” as in someone you know only in a digital space, from Twitter or Tumblr."
